The full learning path for the AZ-800: Administering Windows Server Hybrid Core Infrastructure curriculum is
hosted across five separate foundational learning paths on Microsoft Learn.The primary links required to access 
and complete this course include:1. Identity & ManagementActive Directory Deployment: Learn to deploy and manage
domain controllers on-premises and in Azure Virtual Machines via the Deploy AD DS Domain Controllers Path.Hybrid
Identity: Configure cloud sync, password hash synchronization, and cross-premises federation via the Implement
Hybrid Identity Path.Hybrid Management & Arc: Administer virtual machines and physical servers uniformly across
environments using the Manage Windows Server in Hybrid Environments Path.2. Virtualization & NetworkingHyper-V &
Containers: Configure host settings, deploy Windows Server containers, and manage isolated clusters through the
Manage Virtualization & Containers Path.Hybrid Networking: Design cross-premises DNS, implement IP management,
and configure VPN or ExpressRoute lines through the Implement Hybrid Networking Infrastructure Path.3. Storage &
ServicesFile Servers & Storage Spaces: Configure advanced block storage, scale volumes safely, and link data
structures using the Configure Storage and File Services Path.4. Official Resources & Study MaterialsCentral 
Curriculum Page: Review general requirements, scheduling parameters, and self-paced blocks via the primary 
Microsoft Learn AZ-800 Exam Hub.Skills Evaluation Blueprint: Check itemized knowledge sub-domains and criteria
updates directly inside the official AZ-800 Skills Measured Outline.Hands-on Labs Blueprint: Practice code 
commands and review configuration environment step lists hosted on the community Microsoft Learning AZ-800
GitHub Lab Repository.
